<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Replenishment</h2>
<p>Before launching replenishment automation, prove every app in the stack logs email and SMS consent auditably, with purchase events cutting promotional follow-up the moment checkout completes. Replenishment audiences forgive plain creative; they do not forgive promos sent mid-refund or right after checkout.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>No replenishment promos without proof; transactional messages only</td><td>Consent evidence underwrites all replenishment sending</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Lead replenishment newcomers with teaching and social proof</td><td>Premature replenishment offers teach shoppers to wait</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Replenishment reminder with product context; discount withheld</td><td>Protects replenishment profit when purchase intent is hottest</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Pause replenishment promos; switch to post-purchase teaching</td><td>Replenishment suppression protects the new-customer glow</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>No replenishment promos mid-case; resume after resolution</td><td>Service-active replenishment shoppers reject promos</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Prune unengaged replenishment profiles early</td><td>Shields replenishment sender reputation and inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Replenishment texting respects time and frequency rules</td><td>Replenishment SMS complaints cost more per incident</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Replenishment wholesale accounts get dedicated messaging</td><td>Replenishment retail promos can violate B2B terms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Gate replenishment journeys behind address verification</td><td>Low-grade replenishment signups drag deliverability</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Replenishment internal accounts never enter production</td><td>QA replenishment sends distort real performance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Replenishment exceptions stay undocumented-free</td><td>Replenishment consistency beats clever carve-outs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Reconfirm replenishment consent where timestamps are missing</td><td>Timestamp-less replenishment consent is legal exposure</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Replenishment</h2>
<p>Judge replenishment on margin, not attribution. A durable replenishment program absorbs subscription, overages, SMS, capture, creative, agency, and discount costs and still pays. If replenishment tooling eats toward fifteen percent of attributed margin, reduce replenishment scope before optimizing flows.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. Replenishment free tiers look generous until one limit bites — verify which of contacts, sends, branching, or support constrains replenishment first.</p>
