<h2 class="mt-12">Replenishment matchup FAQ</h2>
<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6">
<div><h3>Klaviyo or Shopify Email for replenishment?</h3><p>Replenishment beginners do well on native email; Klaviyo fits when replenishment logic leans on events, catalog data, and segment reporting, with profile billing modeled on replenishment expansion.</p></div>
<div><h3>Omnisend vs Klaviyo for replenishment?</h3><p>Replenishment speed favors Omnisend for lean crews; replenishment depth favors Klaviyo as logic matures. Run the same replenishment journey live on both and compare maintenance hours.</p></div>
<div><h3>Mailchimp or Klaviyo for replenishment?</h3><p>Pick Mailchimp for replenishment when editor comfort and broadcast breadth lead; Klaviyo when replenishment hinges on Shopify event depth — and verify both official pricing pages on replenishment scale.</p></div>
<div><h3>Do I need a separate SMS tool for replenishment?</h3><p>Replenishment rarely needs specialist SMS day one; add it when texts measurably beat email on replenishment. Vet replenishment consent capture, quiet-hour enforcement, and per-text cost first.</p></div>
<div><h3>How should I suppress audiences in replenishment flows?</h3><p>replenishment flows must shed recent purchasers, case-active shoppers, refunds, and unconsented profiles, with replenishment exit logic visible to any auditor — suppression slips outcost quiet weeks.</p></div>
<div><h3>What does replenishment email cost?</h3><p>Costs combine the platform subscription, contact or send overages, SMS credits, template and creative work, and the discount budget your replenishment campaigns consume. Because providers revise plans frequently, check official pricing pages and build an eighteen-month replenishment total — peak season included — before you commit.</p></div>
<div><h3>Which app should a lean team pilot first for replenishment?</h3><p>For replenishment, choose whatever the team masters in a fortnight — native email for plain replenishment sends, a lean ESP once replenishment branching matters. A finished replenishment pilot beats a stalled grand plan.</p></div>
<div><h3>How do I measure replenishment email results?</h3><p>Keep replenishment honest by tracking margin per send, repeat purchase, complaint and unsubscribe rates, plus support load against attributed revenue; a holdout group for replenishment recipients separates real lift from seasonal noise.</p></div>
<div><h3>Can I run replenishment email without an agency?</h3><p>Yes, if the scope stays small. Pick one replenishment journey, document consent and suppression rules, and reuse a simple template system. For replenishment, hire help only if journey complexity, inbox-placement remediation, or peak replenishment volume genuinely exceeds what the team can run.</p></div>
<div><h3>When should I graduate from my first app for replenishment?</h3><p>Graduate the replenishment stack when the team can no longer edit flows safely, segment replenishment audiences by purchase state, or forecast cost at the growing contact count. For replenishment, that moment usually arrives when more than two people maintain flows or when peak campaigns require documented suppression.</p></div>
<div><h3>How much discounting is acceptable for replenishment?</h3><p>Treat discounts as one lever, not the default. For replenishment, test content-led recovery and loyalty first, cap discount depth against margin, and document who can approve exceptions. For replenishment, code-dependence across most revenue means the offer story — not the price — needs repair.</p></div>
<div><h3>Which Shopify data matters most for replenishment?</h3><p>Order and refund state, cart and browse events, consent source, and product availability cover most replenishment decisions. Before layering replenishment branching on events, fire each one in a test purchase and record what every replenishment-relevant field means for both teams.</p></div>
<div><h3>How do I avoid duplicate sends across apps for replenishment?</h3><p>Give one platform ownership of each replenishment journey, document which app sends what, and share suppression lists where the tools support it. During peak season, audit replenishment weekly by sampling customers and listing every replenishment message each one received.</p></div>
<div><h3>What should a replenishment pilot include?</h3><p>Scope the replenishment pilot narrowly — one audience, one or two replenishment journeys, documented suppression, holdout coverage, thirty-day margin review — and agree the replenishment success metric before the first send.</p></div>
</section>
